  "specification": {
    "unique_id": "cpp_api_graphql_hard_007",
    "name": "PaletteFlux GraphQL Studio",
    "description": "PaletteFlux GraphQL Studio is a creative-centric API platform that lets digital artists, game designers, and interactive storytellers programmatically compose, remix, and stream multilayer visual assets through a single GraphQL endpoint while exposing complementary REST views for legacy clients. Built on a rigorously applied Model-View-Controller pattern, the project treats each \u2018creative asset\u2019 (brush stroke, shader node, animation curve, sound layer) as a first-class model object, controlled by command/query services and rendered to multiple representations (JSON, binary texture atlases, GLSL snippets) depending on the requesting client. \n\nThe application demonstrates how an MVC core can power highly interactive, real-time creative workflows: controllers orchestrate command buses for mutating complex scene graphs, while query handlers gather materialized views optimized for pagination, response caching, and cross-version schema evolution. A unified GraphQL schema allows flexible, client-driven traversal through nested asset relationships, whereas curated REST endpoints serve well-defined, cache-friendly snapshots for CDN distribution. Monitoring hooks, authentication guards, and API-gateway patterns ensure production-grade robustness without sacrificing the free-form expressiveness required by artists and tool developers.",
